  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Salis beach is a long sandy beach at the foot of Cap d'Antibes, shallow and close to old Antibes. The tourist office describes it with lifeguard posts, toilets and showers, and a Handi-plage point near the water sports centre.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>No official source says dogs are allowed on this beach. The Handiplage page for La Salis, published by the Antibes Juan-les-Pins tourist office (updated March 2026), states that "dogs are not allowed on the beaches or in the water", except guide dogs for the blind and assistance dogs (on presentation of the official document and vest). Nice-Matin (8 June 2026) also reports that the town reminds visitors that the rules ban animals from public beaches. No municipal order was found online and the tourist office page gives no dates: call the town hall before coming with your dog, especially from June to September, when the beach is supervised from 9am to 7pm.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: if in doubt, favour the Cap d'Antibes coastal path, a stone's throw away, for a walk with your dog.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Old Antibes and its Provençal market are a few minutes away, as is the coastal path along Cap d'Antibes.</p>
